  "term": "Scale of Prodromal Symptoms",
  "definition": "The Scale of Prodromal Symptoms is a symptom-rating scale used to assess prodromal, or early pre-psychotic, symptoms. In the supplied source, it was used to evaluate psychiatric symptoms in people at clinical high risk for psychosis and in healthy controls.",
